      "endpoint": "/p1/dashboard/expression/search-tags",
      "cookies": [
        "access_token",
        "refresh_token"
      ],
      "description": "Searches for available tags to use in an expression.",
      "requestExample": {
        "plant_code_id": "Plant_1",
        "query": "temperature",
        "equipment": "Export Compressor"
      },
      "responseExample": {
        "success": true,
        "message": "Tags retrieved successfully",
        "data": [
          {
            "id": "TAG_TEMP_1",
            "label": "Bearing Temperature",
            "unit": "°C"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "uiConsumers": [
    "src/app/(dashboard)/dashboards/** — the dashboard builder (createDashboard/viewDashboard/createVisual/saveVisual/editVisual/deleteVisual) plus its monitor and create flows.",
    "src/app/(dashboard)/home/workflow-diagram/compressor-details/** (added 2026-07-31) — the compressor board. Previously rendered ENTIRELY from hardcoded arrays (DEFAULT_PARASITIC / DEFAULT_UTILITY_MONTHS / DEFAULT_HYDRAULIC / DEFAULT_AVAILABILITY / SCORE_DATA — a Rule 37 violation); it now binds to this domain through three real calls. _hooks/useCompressorEquipment.js owns equipmentList + equipment/{id}/tags; _hooks/useTagSeries.js owns createVisual."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "COMPRESSOR BOARD BINDING (2026-07-31): GET /p1/dashboard/equipmentList returns assets literally named 'Export Compressor' and 'Reinjection Compressor', which map 1:1 onto the compressor-details page's pre-existing ?train=A|B (Export) and ?train=RA|RB (Reinjection) query param. _utils/trainMeta.js resolveEquipmentForTrain() does that match on id/label substring, falling back to the first equipment so plants that don't follow this naming still render real data instead of an empty board. The user can override the auto-resolved asset via ?equipment=<id>.",
    "ONE CALL PER BOARD, NOT PER PANEL (2026-07-31): visual_config.y_axis accepts an ARRAY of tag ids, and the response returns one entry in 'datasets' per tag sharing a single 'labels.x.values' timestamp axis. The compressor board therefore fetches every signal on screen (KPI tiles + trend chart + health gauge) in ONE POST /createVisual rather than one request per panel. Capped at 8 tags in the UI (TagPicker MAX_SELECTION) to keep a single response readable.",
    "DATASET GAPS (2026-07-31): 'datasets[].data' can contain null / non-finite entries where a tag has gaps. Statistics are computed over a filtered copy ('values'), but CHARTS must plot the unfiltered 'raw' array — filtering first shifts every later point off its timestamp in 'labels.x.values'. See _utils/telemetryStats.js summarizeDataset(), which returns both.",
    "PLANT CODE DEVIATION (pre-existing, recorded 2026-07-31): dashboardService.js resolves plant_code_id itself by reading localStorage 'admin_plant_id' (getStoredPlantCode) instead of receiving it as a parameter from useApp().plantCode. This predates the compressor-board work and is shared by ~8 consumers, so it was left alone rather than changed under that scope. useTagSeries.js does pass plant_code_id explicitly in the createVisual BODY (sourced from useApp().plantCode per Rule 0); the service still derives the QUERY copy from localStorage. Both resolve to the same plant selection today. Worth unifying in a dedicated pass."
  ]
}
